10. A fire, reload or draw pose that is still playing is held against the idle call

   dlls\ts_animation.cpp, CTSAnimation::Animate, the run/idle case -- the per-frame idle (or run) call in
   PostThink holds a fire (0, 8, 9), reload (0x33) or draw (0x34) pose while its sequence plays, as TS 3.0
   does: its case 1/6 tests the LAST activity against those five with the sequence not finished, and then
   keeps that activity as the last one (a1 = the last activity; Animate, ts_i386.so 0x5b470). Before, only
   the aim timer held it, which the standing fire sets and the fire lying down (slide_<dir>_<grip>_shoot)
   does not, so in the same server frame as a shot fired lying down the idle call put the standing
   idle_<grip> pose over it; a client sees only a frame's end state, so steady fire flipped the body between
   lying and upright at the fire rate, which looks like humping the ground. The aim timer still holds what it
   covers besides (the grenade throw). Server-side only: the client does not compile ts_animation.cpp. The
   mp.dll this replaced is kept as mp.dll.bak_proneidle in reTS\binaries\ts\dlls\.


