13. The ammo box after a HUD reset

   Where ResetHUD is sent (CBasePlayer::UpdateClientData, dlls\player.cpp), a gun the player still
   holds now clears its WeaponInfo and WStatus caches (m_iClientWeaponType = -1, m_bWStatusInit =
   false), so it tells the client again what it holds: the client's ammo box and weapon bar are
   emptied by ResetHUD, and the original's server resends nothing until the weapon type changes.
   The weapon_<N> command (TSSelectWeaponType, dlls\ts_gun.cpp) clears the WeaponInfo cache after a
   pick, so choosing the weapon already held sends WeaponInfo again; that repairs a stale ammo box
   with one key press. CTSGun::Reset is unchanged (it stores 0, ts_i386.so 0x70626).
   Pairs with client.dll change 26. Described in reTS\reference\DEVIATIONS.md.


14. A marked Mech is not disarmed and takes no dropped weapon

   dlls\ts_gun.cpp (CBasePlayer::DropWeapon) and dlls\ts_player.cpp (CBasePlayer::PickUpWeapon): while the server cvar
   tsm_loadoutrework is on, a player whose pev->fuser4 is set (ts_matchmode sets it to 1 for a Mech each time it hands the
   kit over, with the match mode on) is neither disarmed by a melee hit (DropWeapon, type -2) nor lets go of a weapon on its own (the drop key,
   drop_<n>), and takes no dropped weapon from the floor (PickUpWeapon with a dropped gun's status). A weapon the plugin
   gives with ts_giveweapon, a map weapon (no status) and a death scatter are not touched. Both tests read the cvar only
   for a marked player. The mp.dll this replaced is kept as mp.dll.bak_preweapon41 in reTS\binaries\ts\dlls\.


15. The Mech rocket's blast pushes the players it leaves alive

   dlls\ts_mechrocket.cpp (MechRocketPush, called by CMechRocket::Detonate after TSExplosion), dlls\game.cpp and game.h: TS
   gives a living player no knockback from a hit (combat.cpp, CBaseMonster::TakeDamage), so the rocket pushes the players
   its blast leaves alive itself. Every living player in the blast's radius that the game rules say the thrower may hurt
   (FPlayerCanTakeDamage: friendly fire off spares a teammate), with a clear line from the blast to the player's centre, on
   MOVETYPE_WALK, gets pev->velocity increased by h9_mechrocket_push (units a second, along the ground away from the middle
   of the blast; a player right on it goes the way the rocket flew) plus h9_mechrocket_lift (units a second, up), both
   scaled by the blast's falloff (full out to a quarter of h9_mechrocket_radius, nothing at the radius), the result held to
   1000 units a second, and FL_ONGROUND cleared when there is a lift. The thrower is pushed only when
   h9_mechrocket_selfdamage is 1; a player the blast kills gets TS's own death launch instead. Two new server cvars,
   h9_mechrocket_push (400) and h9_mechrocket_lift (250); 0 for both is the old behaviour. No weapon-table or interface
   change. The mp.dll this replaced is kept as mp.dll.bak_prepush in reTS\binaries\ts\dlls\. Described in
   reTS\reference\DEVIATIONS.md.

