Building and deploying
----------------------

    cd reTS
    $env:RETS_REBUILD = '1'
    .\scripts\build-win32-dropin.ps1

writes binaries\ts\dlls\mp.dll and binaries\ts\cl_dlls\client.dll. xash.bat's assemble step
sets RETS_REBUILD=1 itself, so the H9XASH package takes this pair rather than the older
release_binaries pair. Without RETS_REBUILD=1 the script copies release_binaries\ts\ -- the
shipped release DLL with binary patches A and B (see the appendix) -- and none of the changes
above is present.

The GoldSrc package does not take this pair yet: while reTS\binaries\goldsrc\ holds a pair,
export.bat's GoldSrc block copies that one into export\ts\, the last pair built for 32 player
slots (mp.dll 988672 bytes, SHA256
ADE12259BFAB0EB780E27D397FC3A74DFE003BD74A362D8F8C04A1EE421BA742), and the Steam install keeps
it. This pair goes there once it has passed the regression tests at 32
(docs\PLAYER_LIMIT_128.txt, section 23) and reTS\binaries\goldsrc\ is removed.


